# Desktop overlay UX

## Shape and surface
- One cream `#shell` that morphs — do not add a separate left cream card beside the session rail.
- Boxy rounded corners (`~14px`), not pill/`border-radius: 999px` on the shell.
- Session-time rail stays on the docked edge (right/left/top): green fill grows with study progress; no grey XP track or level badge.

## Open / close motion
- Prefer function-driven stages over stepped frame `setBounds` loops.
- Open (sides): content square matches closed strip length; outer width adds `barThickness` for the session rail, then fade content in.
- Open (top): grow thickness to content square + rail, then widen along the edge.
- Close: fade content out, then reverse (narrow; top also shortens).
- Use native `setBounds(bounds, true)` on macOS when motion is allowed; respect reduced motion (instant bounds, no waits).
- Keep `panelToggleSeq` so rapid toggles cancel stale timeouts.

## Pet
- Closed bar: anchor the pet beside the session rail (`barThickness`).
- Open bar: hide the external pet window and show the pet inside the cream shell; restore the external pet when closing a distracted tab (walk animation).
- Drag from the pet only (closed external sprite or open in-panel sprite); the session rail opens/closes the bar; no drag handle; no bottom dock target (left/right/top only).
- Chat bubbles sit above the pet with a sharp triangle tip (fade in). Live distraction / close copy show for open or closed; open-bar-only idle lines stay in-panel.

## Do not
- Invent XP or change session/score APIs for overlay polish.
- Leave a large transparent window after close that blocks other apps.
